abstract: '<p>This repository contains SynthADAs, a synthetic database of multimodal
  electrophysiological signals associated with Anxious-Depressive Attacks (ADAs).
  The signals include electrocardiography (ECG), bilateral electromyography (EMG)
  of the left and right trapezius muscles, electrodermal activity (EDA), body temperature,
  and respiration waveform.</p>

  <p>The database simulates 100 subjects across four phases: Neutral, Transition,
  Induction, and Recovery. The signals were generated by adapting reference parameters
  reported in the literature for conditions related to ADAs, including Obsessive-Compulsive
  Disorder, Generalized Anxiety Disorder, Panic Disorder, induced stress, and stress
  exposure in high-demand clinical environments.</p>

  <p>The data are provided as 400 CSV files, one per subject and phase (100 subjects
  &times; 4 phases). Each file contains 12,000 samples across seven columns: a timestamp
  and six signal channels.</p>'
